diff --git a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
index 686586363..8820c45d3 100644
--- a/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
+++ b/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Main_Changes_Guide.md
@@ -249,7 +249,7 @@ Note 2: Master–vassal(s) changes are intended to strengthen overall AI play by
 - **Musketmen — AI role**: now also flagged with `UNITAI_ATTACK_CITY`, so the AI uses Musketmen more often in **offensive city-assault** roles. Civ-specific Musketman variants may also include additional changes.
 - **Grenadiers & Bazookas — AI role**: now also flagged with `UNITAI_CITY_DEFENSE`, so the AI may use them more for **city defense**.
 - **War target selection — distance guard**: added a **distance-based pre-filter** in `Risk::preEvaluate` (WarUtilityAspect.cpp) so the AI **rejects faraway rivals** during war-risk evaluation. This curbs "bait" wars that leave cores under-defended and keeps armies concentrated near relevant fronts. See [KI#61](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#61---seemingly-tremendously-improved-ais-getting-baited-to-attack-faraway-rivals-leaving-their-core-cities-mostly-defenseless-but-and-oftentimes-dying-shortly-after-to-an-opportunistic-rivals-changed-by-adding-a-pre-filter-reject-in-war-risk-assessment-based-on-distance-to-us-in-riskpreevaluate-in-warutilityaspectcpp).
-- **City evacuation — doomed city auto-retreat (land units only)**: in `CvUnitAI::AI_evacuateCity`, the AI now **evacuates 100% of its land units** from a **doomed city**. Previously it often retreated only a tiny fraction (e.g., 2 of 11 defenders vs a 22+ stack, whereas now all 11 defenders would evacuate if the city is deemed doomed). This change might prolong wars/game length (although it is not tested beyond the sample case to know for sure if it would be so), but the intent is a **more competitive, less self-sabotaging** AI. See [KI#62](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#62---extremely-betterstronger-ai-almost-not-evacuating-at-all-doomed-cities-2-swordsmen-in-an-11-unit-defending-stack-vs-a-22-attacking-unit-stack-fixed-by-always-and-100-evacuating-city-doomed-city-regardless-of-land-unit-type-in-cvunitaiai_evacuatecity).
+- **City evacuation — doomed city auto-retreat (land units only)**: in `CvUnitAI::AI_evacuateCity`, the AI now (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5464+) optionally (default ON, recommended) **evacuates 100% of its land units** from a **doomed city**. Previously it often retreated only a tiny fraction (e.g., 2 of 11 defenders vs a 22+ stack, whereas now all 11 defenders would evacuate if the city is deemed doomed). This change might prolong wars/game length, but the intent is a **more competitive, less self-sabotaging** AI. See [KI#62](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#62---extremely-betterstronger-ai-almost-not-evacuating-at-all-doomed-cities-2-swordsmen-in-an-11-unit-defending-stack-vs-a-22-attacking-unit-stack-fixed-by-always-and-100-evacuating-city-doomed-city-regardless-of-land-unit-type-in-cvunitaiai_evacuatecity).
 - (Requires AdvCiv-SAS 5405+) **Minimum Stack size before war**: Added a minimum stack unit count requirement to prevent the stack from being marked as "ready" until it has enough units: no `MOVE_DECLARE_WAR` flag, no premature advance toward the city, and AI keeps building units until the stack is big enough. Helps fix the issue of "back and forth" war declarations with immediate retreat without city attack: low-numbered unit stacks were especially sensible to power swings (city defenses, one more enemy units skews win chance, etc.). Change in `CvUnitAI::AI_attackCityMove`. See [KI#104](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#104---tremendously-improved-base-advciv-issue-of-the-weird-back-and-forth-of-declaring-war-moving-a-stack-then-withdrawing-without-attacking-which-is-extremely-inefficient).
 - **City attack oscillation — pre-check vs strong targets (possible mitigation)**: In `CvUnitAI::AI_attackCityMove`, add a sanity check to **skip marching to/attacking a city** when the **defending stack is too strong**. Goal: prevent the inefficient **advance → abort → backtrack** loop and reduce the risk of being caught without time to retreat. **Note:** in the test sample, this behavior also resolved without the change by running ~2+ autoplay turns in a row instead of 1 turn only from a slightly older save file rather; treat this as a **possible fix/sanity check** (not (at least not yet) broadly tested). See [KI#63](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#63---possibly-prevented-and-possibly-fixed-weird--very-inefficient-back-and-forth-of-going-to-attack-a-city-stack-and-then-going-back-after-seeing-enemy-stack-is-too-strong-i-dont-know-if-this-change-fixes-it-since-the-issue-was-solved-without-it-2-autoplay-turns-were-needed-at-least-it-seems-not-1-but-maybe-this-change-in-cvunitaiai_attackcitymove-helps-a-lot-but).
 - **Early-game razing — distance-aware captures**: Updated conquer/raze logic so that, for roughly the first **~120 turns** (scaled by game speed), the AI **razes captured cities** that aren’t **close enough** to justify early investment, in `CvPlayerAI::AI_conquerCity`. This addresses the base AdvCiv pattern where forces overextend (most troops sit in a faraway capture while **core cities** thin out) and also preserves scarce early economy (city maintenance, low pop, time to build improvements/culture). Indirect effect: less fog-busting far from us → **more barbarians** there, which tends to pressure rivals. Net: a **stronger, more focused** early AI (fewer "split in two" empires). See [KI#64](/_1_AdvCiv-SAS/Docs/README_Known_Issues_In_Base_AdvCiv_Civ4.md#64---greatly-enhanced-ai-not-razing-faraway-cities-at-captures---now-we-raze-them-if-we-are-in-the-early-game-and-they-are-not-close-enough-thanks-to-changes-and-tweaks-in-cvplayeraiai_conquercity).

